Bug: request file loses to another scheduled file (macOS only)

prepareInputFileForRequest (src/server.c) prepares the first scheduled file by
fileNumber, which is a hash of the absolute path. When another file is also
scheduled, the wrong one can win, so this fails on macOS and passes on Linux.
The extra file is scheduled only when a header is the request file, so the open
question is what schedules it. Also pinned by the suspended Cgreen test
Server -> prepares_the_request_file_when_others_are_also_scheduled (00a8ded3).
